WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:01.501
-It's always a joy

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.100
to see both of you.

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:05.801
Thank you for being here
on our Fallontine's Day show.

00:00:05.801 --> 00:00:08.868
When I think of a bromance,
I think of you guys.

00:00:08.868 --> 00:00:10.434
-Thank you, Jimmy.
-We appreciate that.
-Yeah.

00:00:10.434 --> 00:00:13.367
[ Laughter ]
You guys have been friends
for nearly 40 years.

00:00:13.367 --> 00:00:14.834
-Yeah.
-We talked about this
on the show.

00:00:14.834 --> 00:00:17.968
You were in detention
in grade school.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:17.968 --> 00:00:20.100
Here you are in seventh grade.
Look at this.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:21.934
[ Awws ]
-So studious.

00:00:21.934 --> 00:00:23.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:23.701 --> 00:00:26.300
-What is the secret to such
a long-lasting friendship?

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:27.968
Have you ever had fights
or conflicts?

00:00:27.968 --> 00:00:29.234
-Well, we're actually --
We're kind of going through

00:00:29.234 --> 00:00:30.767
something right now,
to be honest with you,

00:00:30.767 --> 00:00:34.067
[ Laughter ]
because Link, in a mountain,
biking accident

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:35.868
broke his collarbone
in December,

00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:39.334
so, he's basically fully
recovered, but he wore a sling.

00:00:39.334 --> 00:00:40.968
-Yeah, I was wearing a sling
for like

00:00:40.968 --> 00:00:42.834
the whole month of January
on the show.

00:00:42.834 --> 00:00:45.167
-Right. And what I realized,
at the time --

00:00:45.167 --> 00:00:46.467
and this is the source
of the conflict --

00:00:46.467 --> 00:00:48.534
is that, when I get excited

00:00:48.534 --> 00:00:49.868
about something that's happening
on the show --

00:00:49.868 --> 00:00:51.334
and, of course,
we sit as Rhett &amp; Link,

00:00:51.334 --> 00:00:53.400
so nobody gets confused, just
like we're doing right now --

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.868
[ Laughter ]
I'll hit him in the shoulder.

00:00:55.868 --> 00:00:57.334
I'm, "Hey!" You know,
I'm having a good time.

00:00:57.334 --> 00:00:58.834
I'm punching my buddy, you know?
-Yes.

00:00:58.834 --> 00:01:02.200
-And I realized I actually --
I hit him quite a lot.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:04.400
[ Laughter ]
-And he had his --
And you were wearing a sling.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:06.234
-Yeah.
-Guy's got a broken collarbone.

00:01:06.234 --> 00:01:08.667
-So, I've been trying to find
like a new approach

00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:11.467
to like connect, you know.

00:01:11.467 --> 00:01:13.267
-See, your reaction's
getting better.

00:01:13.267 --> 00:01:15.200
-Yeah. Yeah.
-I mean, you're getting
really good.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:16.400
[ Laughter ]
-Now that I've gotten rid
of the sling,

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:17.501
I've finally gotten good at it.

00:01:17.501 --> 00:01:19.133
-Like a wax on/wax off type
of thing.

00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:20.734
-Yeah, but I haven't really
landed on anything

00:01:20.734 --> 00:01:23.234
because this feels
a little bit weird.
-Yeah, don't do that.

00:01:23.234 --> 00:01:25.968
-You said you got a little kind
of testy, having this sling.

00:01:25.968 --> 00:01:27.934
-I did, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:27.934 --> 00:01:30.367
-I got a little antsy.
I wanted to get out of it.

00:01:30.367 --> 00:01:34.234
Actually, I'd planned, like
the last day I had to wear it,

00:01:34.234 --> 00:01:36.434
we were shooting
"Good Mythical Morning"

00:01:36.434 --> 00:01:38.734
and I said, "I'm just going
to Hulk out of this thing.

00:01:38.734 --> 00:01:39.868
I'm not going to tell Rhett
about it.

00:01:39.868 --> 00:01:41.234
It's going to be
a big surprise.

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:46.567
It's going to be just this
huge moment for our audience

00:01:46.567 --> 00:01:49.267
and for Rhett,
for me to just break out!"

00:01:49.267 --> 00:01:51.534
-Yeah.
-But it didn't --

00:01:51.534 --> 00:01:53.133
It wasn't as easy
as I thought it was going to be.

00:01:53.133 --> 00:01:54.400
[ Laughter ]
-It wasn't as smooth
as that, no.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:56.334
I want to show you.
Here's Link trying

00:01:56.334 --> 00:01:58.968
to Hulk out of his sling.
Check this out.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.968 --> 00:02:01.234
-[ Breathing deeply ]

00:02:01.234 --> 00:02:03.801
Aaaaaaaaaaaaah!

00:02:03.801 --> 00:02:06.834
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.834 --> 00:02:07.968
Aah!

00:02:07.968 --> 00:02:12.100
Aaaaaaaaaaaaah!

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:15.033
Aah! Aah! Aaaah!

00:02:15.033 --> 00:02:16.167
[ Laughter ]
Aah!

00:02:16.167 --> 00:02:18.267
Aaaaaaah!

00:02:18.267 --> 00:02:20.133
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:02:20.133 --> 00:02:21.767
-[ Laughs ]
Your reaction.

00:02:21.767 --> 00:02:23.834
-Hey, listen, if he's anything,
he's subtle.

00:02:23.834 --> 00:02:25.767
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah. You're currently

00:02:25.767 --> 00:02:28.300
in Season 23
of "Good Mythical Morning."

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:31.200
-Thank you.
-You have 11 billion views

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:32.534
across all channels.

00:02:32.534 --> 00:02:35.267
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Crazy.
-Congratulations.

00:02:35.267 --> 00:02:36.934
You have a new new thing
that you've been doing,

00:02:36.934 --> 00:02:39.601
that is almost like a talent
that you think that you have.

00:02:39.601 --> 00:02:40.968
-Yes.
-A special talent.

00:02:40.968 --> 00:02:43.801
-Actually, today's episode
of "GMM"...

00:02:43.801 --> 00:02:47.834
-It just dropped.
-...we brought out
a panel of people

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:51.634
and we said that we could
identify best friends.

00:02:51.634 --> 00:02:53.734
You know, I mean, because we've
been best friends so long,

00:02:53.734 --> 00:02:55.100
we can, you know, we spot them.

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:56.534
[ Snapping fingers ]
Almost instantaneous.

00:02:56.534 --> 00:02:58.667
-And it turns out
we actually could not.

00:02:58.667 --> 00:03:02.200
[ Laughter ]
In fact, we failed
in every single opportunity

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:04.601
and so we thought maybe tonight

00:03:04.601 --> 00:03:06.300
we could have a chance
at redemption

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:08.767
and you could join us and see
if you're any better than us

00:03:08.767 --> 00:03:11.501
at spotting best friends.
-Alright.

00:03:11.501 --> 00:03:13.667
-Look in the audience.
-So can we go in the audience

00:03:13.667 --> 00:03:16.200
and see two people?

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:17.734
Just find two people, random.

00:03:17.734 --> 00:03:20.868
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:03:20.868 --> 00:03:22.567
Alright, alright,
now don't say.

00:03:22.567 --> 00:03:23.634
Alright, alright.

00:03:23.634 --> 00:03:25.100
Alright, now,
what do we have to do?

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:27.801
We have to decide
if they're strangers,

00:03:27.801 --> 00:03:31.868
best friends, or friends?
-They could be lovers, you know.

00:03:31.868 --> 00:03:33.367
[ Laughter ]
-We don't know.
-It's Valentine's Day.

00:03:33.367 --> 00:03:35.033
-Do you have
to ask them questions?
-Yeah.

00:03:35.033 --> 00:03:36.567
-Well, could you guys
just kind of

00:03:36.567 --> 00:03:38.601
make eye contact
with one another?

00:03:38.601 --> 00:03:39.834
-I don't know.
They can't really do it.

00:03:39.834 --> 00:03:41.534
-Okay, they're very smiley,
giggly.

00:03:41.534 --> 00:03:43.267
Okay, if you were coming back
from a long trip

00:03:43.267 --> 00:03:44.534
and you were greeting
one another,

00:03:44.534 --> 00:03:45.801
how would you greet one another?

00:03:45.801 --> 00:03:48.167
Just, you know, physically.

00:03:48.167 --> 00:03:50.868
[ Laughter ]
Oh, yeah, they're definitely
best friends.

00:03:50.868 --> 00:03:52.100
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:53.334
It's written all
over their faces.

00:03:53.334 --> 00:03:55.934
-I would say that I'm not sure.

00:03:55.934 --> 00:03:57.234
I'm not sure they know
each other.

00:03:57.234 --> 00:03:59.334
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
-They are not even acquainted.

00:03:59.334 --> 00:04:02.501
-You think? These people did not
know each other until tonight.
-At all.

00:04:02.501 --> 00:04:04.434
[ Laughter ]
-That's what I'm saying.

00:04:04.434 --> 00:04:05.901
-Is that true?
-What about you?
-Yep.

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:08.701
-We do know each other.

00:04:08.701 --> 00:04:10.067
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.067 --> 00:04:12.601
-Well, act like it!
-Is everything okay?
-Yeah.

00:04:12.601 --> 00:04:15.300
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:16.367
-Alright, let's try again.
Look.

00:04:16.367 --> 00:04:18.634
You didn't redeem yourself.
-Okay.

00:04:18.634 --> 00:04:19.968
Give us another chance.

00:04:19.968 --> 00:04:21.534
-Let's find two other people

00:04:21.534 --> 00:04:22.701
and see if we can try
this again.

00:04:22.701 --> 00:04:24.133
Where else can the camera go?

00:04:24.133 --> 00:04:26.467
[ Cheering and applause ]
Those guys?

00:04:26.467 --> 00:04:29.033
-Here we go. Yeah.
-Okay.

00:04:29.033 --> 00:04:32.367
Okay. There kind of matching,
in an odd way.

00:04:32.367 --> 00:04:35.968
-Can we see, you know,
your secret handshake?

00:04:35.968 --> 00:04:38.300
[ Laughter ]

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:39.300
-We don't have one.

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:40.100
-Make one up.

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:42.400
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.434 --> 00:04:48.067
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:48.067 --> 00:04:49.400
[ Cheering and applause ]
Not bad.

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:51.234
-That was a good
secret handshake.

00:04:51.234 --> 00:04:53.534
It's good. It's so secret,
they don't even know it.

00:04:53.534 --> 00:04:55.501
[ Laughter ]

00:04:55.501 --> 00:04:57.000
-How would you guys
greet one another,

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:59.434
if you had been apart
from each other for, you know,

00:04:59.434 --> 00:05:02.567
hadn't seen each other in a year
and you're reunited,

00:05:02.567 --> 00:05:06.767
you see each other after a year.
How would you embrace?

00:05:06.767 --> 00:05:07.701
-[ Scoffs ]
How would you embrace?

00:05:07.701 --> 00:05:09.968
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:05:09.968 --> 00:05:14.234
[ Rimshot ]

00:05:14.234 --> 00:05:16.501
-I say --

00:05:16.501 --> 00:05:18.167
I say they're
-Strangers!

00:05:18.167 --> 00:05:20.534
-strangers. Strangers!
-Strangers!
-Never met.

00:05:20.601 --> 00:05:22.334
-Never met. Never met.
-Never met.

00:05:22.334 --> 00:05:23.501
Will never talk again.

00:05:23.501 --> 00:05:24.934
[ Laughter ]

00:05:24.934 --> 00:05:27.200
Never speak another word
to each other.

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:29.133
-I think you might
redeem yourselves.

00:05:29.133 --> 00:05:31.067
What do you think?
Do they know each other?

00:05:31.067 --> 00:05:32.934
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:05:32.934 --> 00:05:34.400
-Yeah.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:37.767
I think they might be
in a relationship.

00:05:37.767 --> 00:05:40.834
-Alright.
Are you guys in a relationship?

00:05:40.834 --> 00:05:43.100
-Yes.
-Yes!

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:44.367
-We just got engaged.

00:05:44.367 --> 00:05:45.934
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Oh, my!

00:05:45.934 --> 00:05:49.400
[ Rimshot ]

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:51.734
-Happy Fallontine's Day!

00:05:51.734 --> 00:05:54.667
The very talented Rhett &amp; Link.

00:05:54.667 --> 00:05:55.767
Congratulations.

00:05:55.767 --> 00:05:57.567
All episodes
of "Good Mythical Morning"

00:05:57.567 --> 00:05:59.200
are available on YouTube.

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:01.467
We'll be right back with more
"Tonight Show."

00:06:01.467 --> 00:06:04.567
[ Cheering and applause ]
[ The Roots playing funk ]

00:06:04.567 --> 00:06:06.634
-♪ Uh-huh, uh-huh, uh-huh,
uh-huh, uh-huh ♪

